WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.670
In the 2010s, Arctic sea ice in September
covered about 40 per cent less area

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.030
than in the years 1979 to 88.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:15.170
A 2008 USGS estimate put 90 billion
barrels of undiscovered oil north of the

4
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.670
Arctic Circle.

5
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.830
Russia, Denmark and Canada have each
made submissions to a UN commission.

6
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.270
Parts may overlap.

7
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:28.370
At their heart lies the Lomonosov
Ridge, a sliver of continental crust.

8
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.270
So who owns the ocean floor?

9
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.170
Whoever plants a flag first?

10
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.970
In this mission, you'll draw
the Law of the Sea zones,

11
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.890
out from the coast.

12
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.110
Then you'll weigh the
push for seabed minerals,

13
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.130
with a 1979 mining test revisited in 2023.

14
00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.770
Your mission: find out
who owns the ocean floor.
